    "text": "{\"anomaly_detected\": true, \"confidence\": 0.85, \"anomalies\": [{\"category\": \"short_to_ground\", \"components\": [\"Q1\", \"J1\", \"J2\", \"J5\"], \"pins\": [\"Q1.3\", \"J1.29\", \"J2.29\", \"J5.1\"], \"nets\": [\"GND\", \"Net-(J5-Pin_1)\"], \"observed\": \"The battery-switch P-MOSFET drain (Q1 pin 3, D) is on the GND net, not on a /BAT net. Bus pin 29 on both J1 and J2 is also on GND. No /BAT net exists in the netlist. The battery connector's positive terminal (J5 pin 1) is wired to the Q1 source, so the battery positive is effectively connected to ground through Q1's drain-source/body diode.\", \"expected\": \"The spec says Q1 gates the battery connector onto the /BAT net, which is wired to pin 29 of the M5Stack bus connectors (J1/J2). Pin 29 should be a /BAT net, separate from GND, and Q1's drain should drive that net.\", \"evidence\": [{\"source\": \"netlist\", \"quote\": \"(node (ref \\\"Q1\\\") (pin \\\"3\\\") (pinfunction \\\"D\\\") (pintype \\\"passive\\\"))\"}, {\"source\": \"netlist\", \"quote\": \"(node (ref \\\"J1\\\") (pin \\\"29\\\") (pinfunction \\\"Pin_29\\\") (pintype \\\"passive\\\"))\"}, {\"source\": \"netlist\", \"quote\": \"(node (ref \\\"Q1\\\") (pin \\\"2\\\") (pinfunction \\\"S\\\") (pintype \\\"passive\\\"))\"}, {\"source\": \"spec\", \"quote\": \"The battery connects at J5, through Q1 (IRLML6402 P-MOSFET) acting as a high-side disconnect switch, onto the `/BAT` net, which is wired straight to pin 29 of the M5Stack bus connectors (J1/J2)\"}], \"impact\": \"The battery is short-circuited to ground through Q1's body diode whenever the battery is connected, regardless of the switch. The battery cannot be switched or used to power the Core, and the battery and wiring are at risk of overheating or damage. The M5Stack BAT path is also lost.\", \"confidence\": 0.85}], \"summary\": \"The battery path is wrong: Q1's drain and bus pin 29 (which the spec defines as the BAT pin) are on GND, so the battery positive is shorted to ground through Q1, which defeats the high-side disconnect design.\"}",
